{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20372",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.26,
      "end_seconds": 5.85,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "Okay, come in, have a seat by the desk."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 8.88,
      "end_seconds": 12.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Hello, thanks for fitting me in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 12.64,
      "end_seconds": 16.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "Okay, what would you like to start with today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 18.45,
      "end_seconds": 26.37,
      "duration_seconds": 7.92,
      "text": "It's my heart racing. I thought I'd wait, um, but it hasn't gone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.01,
      "end_seconds": 30.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "How many days or weeks has it been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.51,
      "end_seconds": 36.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Erm, for about three months, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.85,
      "end_seconds": 52.35,
      "duration_seconds": 9.5,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.56,
      "end_seconds": 68.29,
      "duration_seconds": 14.73,
      "text": "About a four out of ten. I'd say all the time. It's worse with stress. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.29,
      "end_seconds": 72.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "Any other symptoms with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.18,
      "end_seconds": 110.25,
      "duration_seconds": 37.07,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get a fluttering in my chest as well. The fluttering in my chest? That's been for four weeks. Sorry, what was I saying, as for fluttering in my chest, a four out of ten, I suppose. I've had being short of breath during an episode too, for four weeks. Well, about being short of breath during an episode, it happens every other day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.12,
      "end_seconds": 116.14,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "Any chest pain, leg swelling or weight loss at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.77,
      "end_seconds": 122.89,
      "duration_seconds": 5.12,
      "text": "No, no chest pain, leg swelling or weight loss."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.58,
      "end_seconds": 125.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "And fainting, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.45,
      "end_seconds": 127.98,
      "duration_seconds": 1.53,
      "text": "No fainting, thankfully."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.7,
      "end_seconds": 132.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "How are your joints, any aches elsewhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.06,
      "end_seconds": 135.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "I move fine otherwise."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.99,
      "end_seconds": 152.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "Tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.98,
      "end_seconds": 160.92,
      "duration_seconds": 6.94,
      "text": "Okay, so it's gliclazide, 80 milligrams, twice a day for my sugar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.33,
      "end_seconds": 173.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "Before we go further, any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.78,
      "end_seconds": 181.74,
      "duration_seconds": 5.96,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, no, nothing as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.79,
      "end_seconds": 184.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.18,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.32,
      "end_seconds": 192.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "No, I've never been operated on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.66,
      "end_seconds": 197.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Alright, what about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 198.23,
      "end_seconds": 202.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.29,
      "text": "Uh, I have diabetes, for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.19,
      "end_seconds": 216.01,
      "duration_seconds": 11.82,
      "text": "I see, go ahead. Yes, diabetes is known to us, good to have that clear. Let's talk a little about your daily life and habits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 217.87,
      "end_seconds": 227.18,
      "duration_seconds": 9.31,
      "text": "My partner and our baby. I'm vegetarian and have been for years. I do a yoga class on Thursdays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.22,
      "end_seconds": 230.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Let's start with the basic checks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.51,
      "end_seconds": 243.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "Bear with me while this finishes..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.21,
      "end_seconds": 262.91,
      "duration_seconds": 6.7,
      "text": "Okay: pulse is 120 beats a minute, pressure 138 over 82, temperature is 37.1 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 263.55,
      "end_seconds": 265.21,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.86,
      "end_seconds": 270.87,
      "duration_seconds": 5.01,
      "text": "Alright, they help me see the whole picture, more shortly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.06,
      "end_seconds": 276.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "Let me look at the area, I'll be gentle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.21,
      "end_seconds": 280.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "Right, I'm just checking this side."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.98,
      "end_seconds": 302.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "The pulse is irregular, around ninety beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 319.76,
      "end_seconds": 320.46,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.41,
      "end_seconds": 342.55,
      "duration_seconds": 18.14,
      "text": "Please sit back down. Okay, so my impression is this: My working impression is paroxysmal palpitations, possibly an atrial arrhythmia. I'd also keep an overactive thyroid in mind. Let's get a heart monitor for a few days, for palpitations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 343.5,
      "end_seconds": 345.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "Is that done today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 346.86,
      "end_seconds": 380.76,
      "duration_seconds": 33.9,
      "text": "I think an ECG makes sense here, for palpitations. We'll begin with bisoprolol, 2.5 milligrams, once a day, until review. It's for heart rate control. I'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it. Cut right back on coffee, tea and energy drinks for now. Avoid taking any extra painkillers on top of what I'm prescribing without checking with us. Come back in three weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 382.33,
      "end_seconds": 386.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "So, anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 388.54,
      "end_seconds": 390.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Thank you, doctor, goodbye."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 391.62,
      "end_seconds": 392.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "All the best."
    }
  ]
}